{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_06c3553dcda7bab8ab137a0a034ca23fff1ac0c2d8d332b5e4e83eb12814956d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_765c39cc93cbc1f5c772fad961380bdaf13987d95647d49f331c4d49d669ba9d","slc_7e694baa69cda9669ca2535cef51502b329b96a77efa08c80cdd2e56f6229a96"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"The distillation pipeline (background summarization and graph extraction) is disabled by default to avoid surprise model spend, and running Honeycomb alongside Hivemind is unsupported, though the dashboard offers migration.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0d7a97f48fa79eb9b9198c73c29e71a1566bf737b6d503343957e0d4da72343b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a84c8f67525fcfee820406e708ed124ba53bf0e0d253c96d9b73fabacc45130f","slc_d93b1189b6f5da48b814915108d35f82b6b3066a133c44a9c266efba4a9c8206"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"Besides the CLI, Honeycomb is reachable via the Hive portal dashboard at 127.0.0.1:3853, a bundled MCP server exposing read/resolve and search/mine tools, and a TypeScript SDK with /react, /vercel, and /openai subpath entries.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_165082757878f530c9262761bd432563d42a678a9e9014567c4753cfb4044f67","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8b5e16d679a6b3703c2fd901f52f1cf4bfcd6a17539cfd326b2effc6618ee451","slc_d71440aaad0ea552b545f625cd42579462df2cd48a24d3deeadcaed401bdbae8"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"The product is a long-lived local daemon plus thin clients (hooks, CLI, MCP, SDK); the daemon is the sole process talking to storage, reached over loopback HTTP on 127.0.0.1:3850.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1eabe2b297ce49922c61afb6f35573bf62b246246d33ebd4085916243ca7a1a4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_07b1ecb78a9d2fee25ad3e8e2ea48033e47d0a625d06dc7558a79a8166245cdc","slc_413c306758a79039be2fdb260e5f1ff13505d19fec97d4ede3acb4466d201467","slc_64accbc2c92535fcf117eaad598affcf76cf27fb25dc2b9f1fbe6f7c5fbd2b22","slc_e2dac0991106cdffda9529661ae06742464ae17fabd4488f6aaa558d4ad900a5"],"source_ids":["src_3869145fd6bd50f18a98db6cdaba9830"],"text":"Repository development practice: the codebase is a single-package TypeScript monorepo with tiered import direction (tier N may import only from lower tiers), DeepLake access confined to src/daemon, and esbuild bundling per target entry root.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_41fe9389a72614698ee314e99f5fd384a4a27a3cdfeaacd4355b1a147db58c2b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_281701bf809ddc5810fbc42d1a9de726c0cf73b7521fa016a6e8deface23a074","slc_33d889f04dc15e672e30fe99c6da0f09234e4a452eca0ee5004607d09b2d5063"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"Honeycomb provides shared, persistent memory for AI coding agents: what one harness learns is recallable by others across sessions, tools, devices, and teammates.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_490e412e95f6805f0bb0c89353f39bdcaf712b2e4a887b58c875710520bf3d58","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5cfcdf707e5efcc20a3bc24705bce520369a0538c218befa2bc5e386ef5b199e","slc_cc36172b9d9125cf08e9f85a36311c24f3973235f4241809068544a4b13051fc"],"source_ids":["src_3724b7b08340571c9cb9773b9dd1aa63"],"text":"Repository development practice: releases are automated from AI-written changesets through a gated version bump (minor releases hold for human approval, major blocked), then tag-on-merge, npm publish via OIDC, and Discord notification.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7267a6371ecfcd5c44006fff118690fb1183267cec9a7555503c19b39276a385","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_52e318d8503d73a33cd79ad3d5ab6f15969ead4b9300db414b6452cc495a2d21","slc_d3a4e28d250fa374b67fcad3f2eb4e7af031ad461701d7f565d3aa895c326932","slc_eee4c24e72d1965151f592d52cd79af383f7013c4819f11c8f64d684deb48077"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"A unified honeycomb CLI exposes verbs such as setup, status, login, start/stop, remember, recall, sessions, and uninstall; baseline operational verbs accept --json with exit codes 2/1/0 for malformed usage, runtime failure, and success.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8bd600f44841d38325e762b3cfa68912a8e8c05c7a2ad198ece46daf02b4352f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_224a4e4a0cce32a1c8c31d11969ff7cd3a83a2a1c268b0606e3c664b71dfd68e","slc_dd0d3f82144fe563c893a6113e5ee837805cf72f1b90e4716292451b8aaa3996"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"Storage can be self-hosted against Activeloop's pg_deeplake Postgres extension, pointed at via honeycomb login --endpoint with a postgres:// or https:// URL, without an Activeloop account.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9442bbe46aabaab82ff85d5f9afadf19f3279ed83cd3695cf3021211ca2c283d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a41c224bca67f1e2c38923385bda4e45c367b3883d5f65d0b4304a8271820a6","slc_33698c71f3492f58d21c38b4601e351f950e618e3599f63d7cdaeb97acbf5cd6"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"Repository development practice: npm run ci is the quality gate every change must pass, combining typecheck, duplication detection (jscpd), vitest tests, and a SQL-safety audit.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9a3b259b09a109931c694e197051a1682108e1f4395050d7002c38e3d9436efe","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7e694baa69cda9669ca2535cef51502b329b96a77efa08c80cdd2e56f6229a96"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"The daemon binds loopback only (single machine); cross-device and cross-user sharing happen through Deeplake's org/workspace scope rather than a remote daemon bind.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9a3b97bde017f7ae99b837e55ae76336d9712899fedfda62cee4c69360cc7dd5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8f93e6ffff21dead766e0c2b2b7f536c9677c32c06ab4e2a4402f14e48c213df","slc_defa63aa5f7d20412f83ecb08a40477b713969efffc7f6c855d5183ceb1c0748","slc_fff575bcde06dc898ccc9ddfa0e7477b2cb3455cdce4b87fa154dc9eb105ebdd"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"Honeycomb is built on Activeloop Deeplake (extending the open-source Hivemind agent-memory project), using BM25 lexical plus 768-dim nomic-embed-text-v1.5 semantic search fused by Reciprocal Rank Fusion.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a8500666d1f2648bdb760f6350d8302a160c84114a33f6156cb0b68800aa0df1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8b6938283f2b4cec7e307883ecaa245a3a7115f9a36fee93f73fb4296c2d3dfc","slc_dd0d3f82144fe563c893a6113e5ee837805cf72f1b90e4716292451b8aaa3996"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"The README reports a measured recall@5 of approximately 0.72-0.78 for the hybrid lexical-plus-semantic retrieval, and describes a smoke:golden-path script run against live Deeplake credentials.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ddf6cb96e3ce82a516ff68742ab020fb12e34502691ab1ada66df2a5cfafcbfb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8b6938283f2b4cec7e307883ecaa245a3a7115f9a36fee93f73fb4296c2d3dfc"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"At session start a bounded index of roughly 300-800 tokens of relevant keys is pushed once, with deeper detail pulled on demand rather than injected per turn.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e9c6db1674f7e632776380adbc6cd349d00b47ec659b703616330b430e14a84e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7e694baa69cda9669ca2535cef51502b329b96a77efa08c80cdd2e56f6229a96"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"Embeddings are opt-in: recall defaults to lexical BM25, and enabling the local embedding runtime (~600 MB fetched on first warmup) adds semantic recall; recall silently falls back and never errors when embeddings are unavailable.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fc6f70f475ec8d1675162d04a2fce9bc9c70b2b0e2c5c68439dbb0613555e3cb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"legioncodeinc/honeycomb@c1cb6bf5674c snapshot c3ac5449590e9e74","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_05dcd79013fee99449b00dfb7438d4d745dbe4eae6f507601f309c41785db9b6","slc_8b6938283f2b4cec7e307883ecaa245a3a7115f9a36fee93f73fb4296c2d3dfc","slc_a59d6460afb8476e8b0621575d4e8dd5bd2ad89d10dcaf60a8629f5f1defae8f"],"source_ids":["src_36ef18a78d73569682489ee5fe8db017"],"text":"Memories exist at three tiers: a one-line key, a distilled summary carrying the semantic embedding, and the full raw session dialogue; resolution is a deterministic pointer walk across three Deeplake tables.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:05:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1a91a288aa82444db7b471b4c9ec71e4"}
